Subject: The shape table marks a shape some of whose objects are prototypes

What this does
  - `aot_dump_shapes` first walks the collector's objects once and marks every observed shape that has a live object with `is_prototype` set; the `Q` line of such a shape carries `isproto=1`.
  - The generator drops such a shape from the layout candidates.

Why we need it
  A class's own prototype object (`Sub.prototype`, which gains its methods by assignment) was taken as an instance layout of its parent class: the unit stamped it with a layout id, every method assignment then walked the layout's chain, and an object that is a prototype breaks the layout anyway. On deltablue the two such layouts cost 5 Minstr in the per-site backend (581.2 -> 586.2).

Soundness
  Profiling build only. It reads the object list at the dump, runs no JS and allocates nothing. A shape wrongly marked loses only a layout.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -65313,0 +65314,12 @@
+    /* A shape some live object of which is a prototype (a class's own prototype object, which gains its methods by
+       assignment) is never a layout: bit 1 of aot_prof_seen, printed as `isproto=1`. */
+    list_for_each(el, &rt->gc_obj_list) {
+        JSGCObjectHeader *gp = list_entry(el, JSGCObjectHeader, link);
+        JSObject *po;
+
+        if (JS_GC_TYPE(gp) != JS_GC_OBJ_TYPE_JS_OBJECT)
+            continue;
+        po = (JSObject *)gp;
+        if (po->is_prototype && po->shape->aot_prof_seen)
+            po->shape->aot_prof_seen |= 2;
+    }
@@ -65374,0 +65387,2 @@
+        if (sh->aot_prof_seen & 2)
+            fprintf(f, " isproto=1");
